  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-CO - Promotion of girls&#x2019; Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Diverse Women, Girls, and Marginalized groups fully realize their rights, exercise their leadership, and live a life free from violence, discrimination, and poverty will be implemented in Zamb&#xe9;zia Province in 2 selected districts. The districts will be the Nicoadala and Maganja da Costa) we have been working in past year to ensure that we continue to build from gains achieved. The choice of the 2 districts was intentional according to the criteria discussed with the implementing partners, and it was agreed that the districts of Nicoadala and Maganja da Costa will be the targeted districts in the province of Zambezia. The list of schools will have a combination of schools that we&#x2019;ve already been working with (70%) and new schools. Total number of schools to be benefitted is 30.In Maganja da Costa we shall be working with 1 secondary school.

For the 2024-2025 our focus will placed on  approaches by workingin the Girl&#x2019;s Clubs as girls empowerment agency  and  working in the increasing community members voice and participation and control (school council role) in order to ensure safe schools and challenge social norms and stigma associated with menstruation.

To improve the access and retention of Girls and other vulnerable children to equitable, quality and transformative education
Contribute to fight GBV (premature unions and sexual harassment)

a) Eliminate financial barriers that stop students from attending schools.
b) Provide a safe environment that enables the girls to pursue education.
c) Eliminated harmful social norms that stopped girls from attending school; and

The Project  is aligned with Oxfam in SAF Cluster Strategy Gender Justice Programme Strategy (2021-2025) in itsPathway 5:The Goal; of the Gender Justice Programme Strategy is that: Diverse women, girls, and marginalized groups fully realize their rights, exercise their leadership, and live a life free from violence, discrimination, and poverty. The Pathway 5 expects that Girls and other Vulnerable Children attain equitable and transformative education opportunities in terms of enrolment, participation, retention and completion at all levels.</narrative>
  </description>
